<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Ireland announces 170 new jobs in Swords.</title>
<headline>Ireland announces 170 new jobs in Swords.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish enterprise and employment minister Richard Bruton said on Wednesday that a Dutch company was expanding its factory in Swords, creating 170 jobs over the next five years.</p>
<p>Organon, a subsidiary of Dutch-based Akzo Nobel, is to expand its pharmaceutical plant in the town, bringing total employment at the factory to 450 people, Bruton said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
